; potions.eval - what drinking a potion does (transparency Phase 4).
;
; Run:  Dungeon.exe -eval tools\EvalScripts\potions.eval
;
; A MEASUREMENT, not a pass/fail. What a reader is looking for, by section:
;
;   1. A FULL MEMBER IS REFUSED and keeps the potion: "gains nothing".
;   2. THE ANTIDOTES: the minor one halves the poison (`cured 1`, the effect
;      still listed with half its bite), the standard one lifts it.
;   3. EACH POOL: a healing potion moves health, a stamina potion stamina, a mana
;      potion mana - each by what is missing, never past the maximum.
;   4. THE DOWNED DRINK NOTHING (Michael: a potion does not wake them).
;   5. The `drink` row of the one-pipeline readout is non-zero.

logecho on
reset

timescale 0
lockstep on
seed 7
arena open 9 9

echo === 1. a full member is refused ===
consume potion_health 0

echo === 2. the antidotes ===
effect poison 0 3 30
step 2
party
consume potion_antidote_minor 0
party
consume potion_antidote 0
party

echo === 3. each pool ===
party
consume potion_health_minor 0
consume potion_health_greater 0
; Stamina spent by marching (every step bills stamina_step), mana by casting
; with the runes learned and a trained hand so the casts do not fizzle.
forward 6
step 1
party
consume potion_stamina 0
learn 2 fire
learn 2 project
setskill 2 fire 30
cast 2 0 fire project
step 1
cast 2 0 fire project
step 1
cast 2 0 fire project
party
consume potion_mana_minor 2
party

echo === 4. the downed drink nothing ===
; Brand emptied by over-exertion (pipeline.eval section 7's recipe), which by
; design can down him but never kill him.
heal
tp 14 14
face north
spawn skel_warrior 14 13 south
setskill 0 unarmed 12
guard 2 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
swing 0
step 4
party
consume potion_health 0

echo === 5. the ledger ===
pipeline
